            <ArticleTitle>Sciatica and epidural corticosteroid injections.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>49</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>According to trials conducted in hundreds of patients with sciatica, epidural corticosteroid injections have no demonstrated efficacy beyond the placebo effect, either in the short-term or the long-term. However, they expose patients to a risk of sometimes serious neurological adverse effects.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
